{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"The first differential run exposed two concrete issues. Rust left `Result` padding bytes indeterminate while this compiled C implementation zeroes them during compound-literal assignment, so whole-object output differed despite matching fields. Separately, the C `FOREACH` macro uses `count_iter != size`; a negative count does not mean zero iterations and instead runs out of bounds, so that case is undefined and must be removed from the valid configuration table rather than “fixed.” I’m zeroing only the C-observed per-element padding in Rust initialization and correcting that configuration/test boundary."}}
